{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And HaShem strengthened Pharaoh's heart.</b> It is possible that in the first plagues the sorcerers were strengthening his heart, to boast before him in their wisdom, but now they did not come before him, and there was no one helping him and no one supporting him in his folly — only his iniquities that ensnared him. Or Scripture may allude to what our Rabbis explained: in the first plagues the matter was through his own transgression, but now there was a cause from HaShem, as I explained above (7:3). And this is the truth:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:56.916348350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}